# Read by project-trajectory/scripts/check_dupes.py (wired as docs/stack.ini
# [step:dupes]). Each non-comment line is a SUBSTRING matched against a finding's
# line-number-free "a.py == b.py" form; a matched finding is passed. So this file
# is the allowlist AND the census: it records every file-pair that currently
# carries sanctioned/known duplication, and — because it is line-number-free —
# an allowed pair stays allowed as those files grow.
#
# WHY a census, not a fix (owner ruling 2026-07-12, repo-review §1 M6 option (b)):
# the kit's F5 working agreement DELIBERATELY duplicates small stable helpers
# (_utf8_console, the declared-policy readers, argparse/exit boilerplate) so each
# script ships independently copy-able — a shared _kitcommon.py was rejected. That
# policy was unbounded and uncensused; this file bounds it. The gate now fails on
# NEW duplication between a pair NOT listed here, forcing a conscious census edit.
#
# KNOWN LIMITATION (honest): granularity is the file-PAIR, because the finding
# form carries no block identity — so new copy-paste between two files ALREADY
# listed here is not caught. Finer (block-content) censusing would need a
# check_dupes change; out of scope for WI-078, recorded here so it is findable.
#
# MAINTENANCE: when you legitimately add F5 helper duplication to a new pair, add
# the pair here (run check_dupes.py --src project-trajectory/scripts to get the
# exact string). When a decomposition removes an intra-file block below, delete
# its line so the census does not rot into permanent cover.

